{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 18:06:39.969190", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content=\"Based on the diagnosis report: ### Troubleshooting Diagnosis Report\\n\\n#### Network Overview\\nThe network consists of:\\n- **Hosts**: `pc1` (195.11.14.2) and `pc2` (200.1.1.2)\\n- **Routers**: `router1` and `router2`\\n- **Topology**:\\n  - `router1:eth0` connected to `router2:eth0`\\n  - `router1:eth1` connected to `pc1:eth0`\\n  - `router2:eth1` connected to `pc2:eth0`\\n\\n#### Observations\\n1. **Reachability Tests**:\\n   - Ping from `pc1` to `pc2` failed with the error: `Destination Net Unreachable`.\\n   - Ping from `pc2` to `pc1` also failed with the same error: `Destination Net Unreachable`.\\n\\n2. **Routing Table Access**:\\n   - Attempts to retrieve the IP routing tables from `router1` and `router2` failed due to the absence of the `vtysh` command, which is typically used for FRR routing configurations.\\n\\n3. **Host Network Configurations**:\\n   - **pc1**:\\n     - IP: `195.11.14.2/24`\\n     - Default Gateway: `195.11.14.1` (connected to `router1:eth1`)\\n     - Interface `eth0` is up and running.\\n   - **pc2**:\\n     - IP: `200.1.1.2/24`\\n     - Default Gateway: `200.1.1.1` (connected to `router2:eth1`)\\n     - Interface `eth0` is up and running.\\n   - **router1**:\\n     - `eth0`: IP `193.10.11.1/24` (connected to `router2:eth0`)\\n     - `eth1`: IP `195.11.14.1/24` (connected to `pc1:eth0`)\\n     - Both interfaces are up and running.\\n   - **router2**:\\n     - `eth0`: IP `193.10.11.2/24` (connected to `router1:eth0`)\\n     - `eth1`: IP `200.1.1.1/24` (connected to `pc2:eth0`)\\n     - Both interfaces are up and running.\\n\\n#### Findings\\n1. **Connectivity Issue**:\\n   - Both hosts (`pc1` and `pc2`) are unable to communicate with each other. The error `Destination Net Unreachable` suggests that the routers are not properly forwarding packets between the two subnets (`195.11.14.0/24` and `200.1.1.0/24`).\\n\\n2. **Routing Configuration**:\\n   - The routing tables of `router1` and `router2` could not be accessed due to the missing `vtysh` command. This prevents verification of BGP configurations and route advertisements between the routers.\\n\\n3. **Interface Status**:\\n   - All interfaces on the hosts and routers are operational and have valid IP configurations. However, there is no evidence of inter-router communication or BGP route exchange.\\n\\n#### Conclusion\\nThe network exhibits abnormal behavior, primarily characterized by the lack of connectivity between `pc1` and `pc2`. The root cause appears to be related to the routers' inability to forward packets or advertise routes between the subnets. Further investigation into the BGP configurations and inter-router communication is required., please provide the submission. Do not submit if no report available.\" additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={} id='def4fe59-e954-4393-afee-9a9ae7087979'", "model": {"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "chat_models", "openai", "ChatOpenAI"], "kwargs": {"model_name": "kt-gpt-oss-rh014", "temperature": 0.0, "openai_api_key": {"lc": 1, "type": "secret", "id": ["OPENAI_API_KEY"]}, "openai_api_base": "https://dev.kora.kt.co.kr/v2", "request_timeout": 180.0, "max_retries": 2}, "name": "ChatOpenAI"}}
